# Per-eye re-projection of CPU-projected geometry (#72), on the simulated headset: after the two eye draws of a
# stereo frame, mouse picking still reads the head camera's screen data at the interface's size (not the last
# eye's), and the screen-space particles are on the flat frame, where they add light without covering the world.
# The spot is the mvp-items scenario of the test save library (scripts\dev\test-saves\scenarios.txt).
# Run with the save: scripts/dev/smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Sequence tl-reprojection -Save mvp-items (xrs-run.ps1 has no -Save;
# @args is what a run without a save gets: level 1 from its start, where the scene differs)
@sim idle
@args --loadlevel 1

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
setpos 10700 2935 11400; lookat key_base_0005
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert vr.stereo.active eq true

# Picking reads the head camera's screen data at the interface's size; before #72 the clip positions and the
# items' bbox2D were the right eye's at the eye image's size. The key is too thin for the 8 pixel grid of
# pick, so it only shows the box test; the form beside it is found on the grid where the camera sees it
vr-sim head rot 0 -35 0                      # look down at the table
@frames 10
@shot table
pick key_base_0005
@assert pick.target eq key_base_0005
@assert pick.targetSeenInBox eq true
pick blank_form_0001
@assert pick.targetSeenInBox eq true
@assert pick.targetHits gt 0
@assert pick.targetOffset ge 0
@assert pick.targetOffset lt 16

# Screen-space particles: a new spell sends the book icon's FX (PARTICLE_2D). They belong to the flat frame:
# the quad changes, and it covers no more of the eyes than before - additive light has no coverage
@shot fx-before
specialfx newspell 1                           # the script command reads one word after newspell
@frames 6
@shot fx-after
@diff table fx-before lt 0.05 quad             # the quad's own floor between two still shots (0)
@diff fx-before fx-after gt 0.1 quad           # the FX is on the quad (0.56 on a 640x480 quad, 0.21 on 918x689)
@remember covered vr.sim.shots.fx-before.quad.covered
@assert vr.sim.shots.fx-after.quad.covered le {covered+50}
@assert errors eq 0
